// One label anchor per muscle — the polygon centroid (shoelace formula) of
// that muscle's SINGLE LARGEST fragment (by area), not an average across all
// of them. Multi-fragment muscles (abs has 13, hamstrings has 16) would
// otherwise pull a naive average toward whichever side has more small
// slivers, landing the anchor somewhere that isn't visually "on" any one
// piece. Picking the biggest single piece keeps the label sitting on solid,
// clearly-that-muscle color. Same coordinate space as *_PATHS (each side's
// own viewBox units) — consumed by MuscleTierMap.tsx's rank-label rendering.
